text:
Congrats to the Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge: Touch Grass Winners!

We are so excited to announce the winners of the [Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge: Touch Grass](https://dev.to/devteam/join-the-hacktoberfest-open-source-ai-challenge-week-1-touch-grass-2450-in-prizes-across-17-4pom)!

**It was another week of record-breaking turnout**, topping last week's [Hacktoberfest Weekend Challenge](https://dev.to/devteam/join-the-hacktoberfest-weekend-challenge-build-for-a-friend-2450-in-prizes-across-17-winners-1aj5). Thank you all for helping us make these challenges such a success.

Our Touch Grass theme asked you to build something with open-source AI at its core that gets people off the screen and into the world, and you delivered. We saw [a laptop that sends you outside the moment the power cuts out](https://dev.to/dannwaneri/light-don-go-when-nigerias-power-cuts-out-my-laptop-sends-me-outside-38k8), [a field app that turns a walk into an investigation where you go out with a question and come back with evidence](https://dev.to/dj29/wildproof-go-outside-with-a-question-come-back-with-evidence-574e), [a kids' plant treasure hunt that will never let poison ivy count as a win](https://dev.to/anchildress1/side-quests-grow-on-trees-leave-them-where-they-grow-84e), and more than a few apps whose whole goal was to get you to put them down. Many of you took your projects outside and told us how it went, which made reviewing your builds a blast.

Thank you to everyone who participated. Your builds made a strong case for why open innovation matters, from models running locally with no signal to tools that keep your data on your own device.

Now, let's celebrate our winners!

